# Session slots and focus

## Model

- **sys** (`AG_SESSION_SYSTEM = -1`): OS shell only; no app bind. Prompt `(sys) …>`.
  Enter only via `Ctrl+\` / `Ctrl+Alt+Del`. Double tap kills last user app.
- **User slots 0..3** (display 1..4): empty = shell `(N) …>`; occupied = app focus.
- Boot focuses **slot 1** (index 0), not sys.
- Apps are real processes (`ag_session_bind_to` on a user slot only).
- `run` / `fm` refuse on sys; pin launch user slot, spawn `AG_SPAWN_NO_SESSION`, bind.
- AXE load is deferred in `proc_task` (`AG_PS_LOADING`).

## Focus rules

- Ready app owns the screen: **no** console banner on focus.
- Same-slot bind (`shell → app`) still needs foreground + `FOCUS_GAINED` (adopt).
- While `AG_PS_LOADING`, show `enter_loading_view` (Alt-back must not look hung).
- Unfocused apps: no console writes; poll sleeps on timeout (no busy-spin).
- Ignore `QUIT` while unfocused.
- `fg` / Alt+1..4 / Alt+Tab never enter sys; Alt+Tab cycles user slots only.

## Keyboard

- Shell owns keyboard on sys **or** empty focused user slot.
- Supervisor hotkeys work even when an app owns the slot.

## Do not

- Treat sys as user slot 0 / display “1”.
- Allow `run`/`fm`/`fg sys` into the system shell.
- Defer bind until load finishes (Alt race into the wrong slot).
- Restore a generic “focused app” console banner for ready apps.
